module

public import Pilean.PiFormula.Bailey

/-!
# The 35 classes of zero conditions (Theorem E, foundation)

A pattern of the 8-dimensional space `V` is a combination `namedComb q` of the eight named
patterns. For each position `k` the condition `ρ(k) = 0` is a linear condition on `q`. The
119 conditions for `k = 1, ..., 119` fall into 35 classes of proportional linear forms (and
`ρ(0) = 0` always). This file records the classes:

* `clsIdx k` is the class of `k`, `clsForm i q = ∑_t v_{i,t} q_t` the integer linear form of
  class `i`, and `namedComb q k = mu k · clsForm (clsIdx k) q` (`namedComb_class`), with
  `mu k ≠ 0` for `k ≢ 0 (mod 120)`. So `ρ(k) = 0` exactly when the form of its class vanishes
  (`namedComb_eq_zero_iff`).
* The 32 units modulo 120 fall into 4 types, by `c mod 12`: for a unit `c` the conditions at
  `c, 2c, 3c, ...` are those at `c₀, 2c₀, 3c₀, ...` with `c₀ = typeRep c ∈ {1, 7, 11, 17}`
  (`type_table`).

The tables are generated by scripts/egen.py and checked here by `decide +kernel`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Complex

namespace PiFormula

